 ## Overview
-This method computes gradient vectors for volume shading by sampling the 3D texture at positions offset from the current reconstruction sample, thereby avoiding the expensive computation of a separate pre-calculated gradient field [S2]. It is distinct from [Gradient Computation via Finite Differences](1077-gradient-computation-via-finite-differences.md) because it performs the finite difference approximation implicitly during the ray-casting shading pass rather than storing the result in a dedicated array. It differs from [Sobel Operator](1416-sobel-operator.md) by using simple forward/backward offsets along axes rather than a 3x3x3 kernel, and from [Jacobian Estimation via Central Differences](2650-jacobian-estimation-via-central-differences.md) by relying on specific hardware texture sampling offsets provided by the rendering pipeline context.
